      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>MINIMAL DISEASE ANALYSIS FOR HAIRY CELL LEUKEMIA</strong></p>\n<table class=\"Table cke_show_border\" style=\"height: 334.889px; width: 64.8382%;\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.4795%;\">\n<p><strong>Clinical history</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 51.5691%;\">\n<p>K/C/O HAIRY CELL LEUKEMIA</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.4795%;\">\n<p><strong>Specimen</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 51.5691%;\">\n<p>Bone Marrow</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.4795%;\">\n<p><strong>Instrument software</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 51.5691%;\">\n<p>BD FACS LYRIC/BD FACS SUITE</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.4795%;\">\n<p><strong>Gating strategy</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 51.5691%;\">\n<p>10 colour FCM using CD 45 gating.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.4795%;\">\n<p><strong>Cell preparation method</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 51.5691%;\">\n<p>Stain - Lyse - Wash</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 59px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.4795%;\">\n<p><strong>Number of Events Acquired</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 51.5691%;\">\n<p>1200000</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Descriptive summary:</strong><br>Flow cytometric immunophenotypic analysis of the bone marrow was done on CD45/side scatter plots. A total of 12 lac events were acquired.</p>\n<p>Populations of normal lymphocytes, hematogones and other normal marrow elements seen.<br><br>CD19 gating and further hierarchial analysis shows a small cluster of cells with immunophenotype of Hairy Cell Leukemia. These cells constitute 0.007% of all nucleated cells (&lt;0.01%).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;<br><strong>IMPRESSION: Minimal residual disease is negative for a cut off of &ge;0.01%.</strong><br><br></p>\n<p><strong>Note: Repeat evaluation at a later time point (in view of a very small population of cells with abnormal immunophenotype).</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Note:&nbsp;</strong><br>The assay has not been standardised specifically for Hairy cell leukemia. The analysis has been done using protocol similar to the one being used for other MRD assays.</p>\n<p>Antibodies used &ndash; CD45, CD19, CD20, CD200, CD123, CD103, CD305, CD11c, CD25, Kappa, Lambda, CD5, CD10.</p>\n<p>The results are to be correlated with the clinical details, diagnostic immunophenotype and cytogenetic profile of the patient.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "678c8611af0b85d849dc0d26"
    }
  ],
